score_pct: 40.5
findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed the from_file_or_default swallowing all errors. TEA
    tests cover missing file defaults but don't test that parse/permission errors
    are distinguished from NotFound.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented CWE-209 safe Display impls with fixed user-facing messages.\
    \ Reviewer verified: 'Display impls use fixed user-facing messages. Internal details\
    \ are not exposed in Display.' However, no dedicated user_message() method was\
    \ created \u2014 stderr still uses eprintln with Display, so partial catch. Counting\
    \ as caught since the Display impl was sanitized."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CWE-113 header injection tests for tenant ID with CRLF/null\
    \ bytes. Dev implemented validation rejecting \\r, \\n, \\0. However, the deeper\
    \ issue \u2014 using raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core \u2014\
    \ was flagged by Reviewer as MEDIUM: 'The --tenant flag is Option<String> (raw,\
    \ unvalidated) instead of using the TenantId newtype.' Partial catch: injection\
    \ prevented but type-safety gap remains."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. Reviewer noted a toml version mismatch but did not flag the
    workspace dependency pattern violation.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as MEDIUM: ''RawConfig uses serde default deserialization
    which silently ignores unknown fields. A config file containing token = "my-secret"
    is silently accepted and the token is discarded... serde\''s #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]
    would actively reject configs containing a token field.'''
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...). TEA wrote config tests but the specific assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...) pattern was not flagged.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with let _ = config. TEA wrote config_loading tests but this specific test quality
    issue was not flagged.
